#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096558 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbcc16b7-dd31-55ce-ba1e-02b87263453c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Dimension of a Cylinder Given Its Volume"}] :question/id #uuid "e61b5943-210d-5ef3-9c71-5780762b0163" :question/math-academy-id "e-7182" :question/problem "Calculate the radius $r$ of the cylinder below given that its volume is $200\\pi \\,\\textrm{mm}^3$ and its height is $2\\,\\textrm{mm}.$\n\n![](images/d0/d0450b9c0f3ab8b6f5f0cf09c4ca21dac75d0077fe8b44bf740eb4dc198decfe.png)" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV = \\pi r^2h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $V = 200\\pi \\,\\textrm{mm}^3$ and $h = 2\\,\\textrm{mm}$ into the formula and solving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ 200\\pi  & =\\pi {r}^{2}(2) \\\\ 2\\pi {r}^{2} & =200\\pi  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =100 \\\\ r & =10\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096559 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdf7b0cd-95b8-5cc6-94c4-768ec04c973a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Cylinder"}] :question/id #uuid "edf5a890-3d4f-5917-b6a5-b1e3ff055fa3" :question/math-academy-id "e-7185" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of a cylinder given that the circumference of the base is $10\\pi \\,\\textrm{m}$ and the ratio of its height to its radius is $\\dfrac{4}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the radius $r$ using the formula $C=2\\pi r,$ where $C$ is the circumference, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 10\\pi  & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =5\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the height $h,$ we use the fact that the ratio of the height to the radius is $\\dfrac{4}{5} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{h}{r} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{h}{5} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ h & =4\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV = \\pi r^2h .\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r = 5\\,\\textrm{m}$ and $h = 4\\,\\textrm{m}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV = \\pi(5)^2(4) =  100\\pi\\,\\textrm{m}^3 .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096560 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "234b3cbc-1b13-50fc-9bec-e2149cfb2ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Expression for a Dimension of a Cylinder Given a Proportion"}] :question/id #uuid "af065541-e7e0-5f34-a566-40de5b546f0d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7217" :question/problem "Find an expression for the height $h$ of a cylinder in terms of its volume $V$ given that the ratio of the radius of the base to the height of the cylinder is $4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the ratio of the radius $r$ of the base to the height $h$ is $4,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur goal is to express $h$ in terms of $V.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $r$ in the above equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =4 \\\\ r & =4h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV = \\pi r^2 h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $r = 4h$ into the formula and solving for $h,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ V & =\\pi {(4h)}^{2}h \\\\ V & =16\\pi {h}^{3} \\\\ {h}^{3} & =\\frac{V}{16\\pi } \\\\ h & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{V}{16\\pi }}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdf7b0cd-95b8-5cc6-94c4-768ec04c973a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Cylinder"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "414dfa3d-7db0-5f37-ac64-7f0f59cd5b17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553000} {:answer/id #uuid "45a0e5bc-acd8-50a4-b544-ec302eb8872b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553009} {:answer/id #uuid "661019cc-b536-5563-b126-8e4a91119d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553084} {:answer/id #uuid "be3ab9da-0d37-56a4-a53b-3263659abbe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553245} {:answer/id #uuid "e30df005-616f-5013-b647-c1f3fa257838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "343\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be3ab9da-0d37-56a4-a53b-3263659abbe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553245} :answer-field/id #uuid "9944ed2c-3b76-5bfa-8192-ee49f9c9b49e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "848e4810-50fc-59b2-b891-7a6431b7108e" :question/math-academy-id "q-117870" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of a cylinder given that the circumference of the base is $14\\pi \\,\\text{m}$ and the ratio of its height to its radius is $\\frac{1}{49}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the radius $r$ using the formula $C=2\\pi r,$ where $C$ is the circumference, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 14\\pi  & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =7\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the height $h$, we use the fact that the ratio of the height to the radius is $\\frac{1}{49}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{h}{r} & =\\frac{1}{49} \\\\ \\frac{h}{7} & =\\frac{1}{49} \\\\ h & =\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=7\\,\\text{m}$ and $h=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi \\cdot {7}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}=7\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "234b3cbc-1b13-50fc-9bec-e2149cfb2ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Expression for a Dimension of a Cylinder Given a Proportion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406b3ae1-b26a-5f6c-9899-76946ce7cfe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=\\frac{1}{8}\\pi h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552999} {:answer/id #uuid "421a8784-b386-50cc-a2f4-d72aae749d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=\\frac{1}{64}\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553003} {:answer/id #uuid "70819995-5f1f-504a-9a2f-796e854157ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=8\\pi h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553100} {:answer/id #uuid "9c28f259-1765-546e-b571-116f240c5f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=8\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553185} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0c4f57-7a75-5df2-bd6f-aad1b894860c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=64\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd0c4f57-7a75-5df2-bd6f-aad1b894860c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=64\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553307} :answer-field/id #uuid "6828f168-8b35-5454-b18c-be99f62bdfeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "305fc84c-d647-5a56-b2b2-8cf846cd7929" :question/math-academy-id "q-117880" :question/problem "Find an expression for the volume $V$ of a cylinder in terms of its height $h,$ given that the ratio of the radius of the base to the height of the cylinder is $8.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the ratio of the radius $r$ of the base to the height $h$ is $8,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{r}{h}=8.\n$$\n\nOur goal is to express $V$ in terms of $h.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $r$ in the above equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =8 \\\\ r & =8h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $r=8h$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\pi (8h)^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 64{h}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =64\\pi {h}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdf7b0cd-95b8-5cc6-94c4-768ec04c973a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Cylinder"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b17959-4147-5059-a372-6e3f2b81dc48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552962} {:answer/id #uuid "61f153d8-fad3-54f5-b55b-5f79a05485cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "130\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553079} {:answer/id #uuid "c04b462b-927e-5165-81a9-cf451d1c4151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553250} {:answ