eb155b2b36a29769591d89549a9fd.png)\n\nCalculate the volume of a cylinder given that its diameter is $34\\,\\text{m}$ and its height is $11\\,\\text{m}.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{34}{2}=17\\,\\text{m}$ and $h=11\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi (17)^{2}(11)=3\\,179\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbcc16b7-dd31-55ce-ba1e-02b87263453c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Dimension of a Cylinder Given Its Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f9fe2a-0a4d-5175-a120-13f498a8192d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\pi \\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552911} {:answer/id #uuid "2c703f63-eaee-52fe-8bae-7f463f01eb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi \\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552951} {:answer/id #uuid "a75cf625-d26e-5229-ae52-7c80f610b6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi \\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553201} {:answer/id #uuid "cb423bc8-8cca-5c73-bda7-b3136d28efe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\pi \\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553274} {:answer/id #uuid "eea29e9a-ab4d-5b6c-bfa4-29977d690c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi \\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eea29e9a-ab4d-5b6c-bfa4-29977d690c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi \\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553340} :answer-field/id #uuid "de23f58e-b184-5f64-92ed-e2b92b69efb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97018909-a799-5979-822f-383b250a0e77" :question/math-academy-id "q-32465" :question/problem "Calculate the circumference of the base of a cylinder given that its volume is $1\\,536\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}$ and the ratio of its radius to its height is $\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the ratio of the radius $r$ of the base to the height $h$ is $\\frac{1}{3},$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ h & =3r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $V=1\\,536\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}$ and $h=3r$ into the formula, we can find the value of $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ 1\\,536\\pi  & =\\pi {r}^{2}(3r) \\\\ 1\\,536 & =3{r}^{3} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =512 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt[3]{512} \\\\ r & =8\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the formula for the circumference of the base is $C=2\\pi r.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nC=16\\pi \\,\\text{cm}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbcc16b7-dd31-55ce-ba1e-02b87263453c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Dimension of a Cylinder Given Its Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e0a5b34-4019-5f4a-8375-4303ad8f7b4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552955} {:answer/id #uuid "471c5dea-7288-5a56-958f-067580d15baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=2\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553014} {:answer/id #uuid "a93496e4-97c1-5afd-84fd-e7f7ad97ced5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553207} {:answer/id #uuid "d4225406-8293-59b3-af72-40ed3480b4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=4\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553294} {:answer/id #uuid "faba3d5c-7a0d-5929-a968-a619158547ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4225406-8293-59b3-af72-40ed3480b4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "h=4\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553294} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eef6173-ab6c-5870-82d9-2a456dd3ae17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32c3dd6f-214e-5de8-b074-37738b30996f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32475" :question/problem "Calculate the height $h$ of a cylinder given that its volume is $16\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}$ and the ratio of its height to its radius is $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that  the ratio of the height $h$ to the radius of the base $r$ is $2,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{h}{r} & =2 \\\\ r & =\\frac{h}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $V=16\\pi {\\text{ cm}}^{3}$ and $r=\\frac{h}{2}$ into the formula, we find the value of $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ 16\\pi  & =\\pi {(\\frac{h}{2})}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\ 16 & =\\frac{{h}^{3}}{4} \\\\ {h}^{3} & =64 \\\\ h & =4\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "234b3cbc-1b13-50fc-9bec-e2149cfb2ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Expression for a Dimension of a Cylinder Given a Proportion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d93f3da-7de8-5fda-8c73-8d15d9a50060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=5\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552883} {:answer/id #uuid "110a1701-e7bd-59cc-bf23-b909a11121b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=\\frac{1}{25}\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552894} {:answer/id #uuid "15516b73-dbd4-571e-8849-4449a9ef906f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=\\frac{1}{5}\\pi h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552905} {:answer/id #uuid "a9cb207f-f35a-5e63-8c48-197ca08c5649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=5\\pi h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553209} {:answer/id #uuid "e9954c65-5cd7-5942-b40e-b08333573fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=25\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9954c65-5cd7-5942-b40e-b08333573fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "V=25\\pi {h}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553333} :answer-field/id #uuid "c41b396a-9473-5099-880c-97b185b1f2ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30ca3ff5-4f8e-556f-a019-237ca2e9ceb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-82232" :question/problem "Find an expression for the volume $V$ of a cylinder in terms of $h$ given that $\\frac{r}{h}=5,$ where $r$ is the radius of the base and $h$ is the height of the cylinder." :question/worked-solution "Our goal is to express $V$ in terms of $h.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $r$ in the above equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =5 \\\\ r & =5h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $r=5h$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\pi (5h)^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 25{h}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =25\\pi {h}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
